      "body": "🚨 **BLOCKING: broken require path — the module cannot be loaded**\n\n`js/common/bugFixBatchContext.js:10` requires `./configLoader.js`:\n\n```javascript\nvar configLoader = require('./configLoader.js');\n```\n\nBut `configLoader.js` lives at `js/configLoader.js` — one directory **up**. From inside `js/common/`, `./configLoader.js` resolves to the nonexistent `js/common/configLoader.js`. Verified directly: `node -e \"require('./js/common/bugFixBatchContext.js')\"` fails with `Cannot find module './configLoader.js'`.\n\nThis is not cosmetic — per the gh-823 rule in AGENTS.md, top-level (load-time) requires resolve **file-relative**, and `dmtools compile` discovers the pack closure strictly file-relative. So this breaks:\n\n1. **Runtime**: `js/prepareBugFixBatchContext.js:17` and `js/developBugFixBatchAndCreatePR.js` both `require('./common/bugFixBatchContext.js')` — the bug-fix-batch pre/post actions will fail at module load (\"Failed to require module\") in the GraalJS engine.\n2. **Pack build**: `dmtools compile` will fail to close the pack over a nonexistent file.\n\nEvery sibling module in `js/common/` uses the correct `../configLoader.js` (actionTicketContext.js:15, buildEncodedConfig.js:13, contentOutput.js:32, trackers.js:57, etc.) — this one slipped through because the unit tests load the module via `loadModule(..., makeRequire({ './configLoader.js': configLoaderMock, ... }))` (`js/unit-tests/test_developBugFixBatchAndCreatePR.js:51-56`), which maps the literal spec string and never exercises real path resolution.\n\nFix: `require('../configLoader.js')`. Ideally also wire `test_bugFixBatchDevelopment.js` into `run_all.json` (see the related IMPORTANT comment) so real path resolution gets exercised."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "rootCommentId": 4368624100,
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORYAuYs6v78SO",
      "path": "js/unit-tests/test_bugFixBatchDevelopment.js",
      "line": 56,
      "resolved": false,
      "bot": false,
      "body": "⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the only direct coverage of the new shared module never runs in CI**\n\nThis PR extended `js/unit-tests/test_bugFixBatchDevelopment.js` with the tests for the new `js/common/bugFixBatchContext.js` helper — but that test file is **not in `js/unit-tests/run_all.json`** (checked: 216 entries, `test_bugFixBatchDevelopment.js` absent), so the full-suite gate never executes it. This is why the broken `require('./configLoader.js')` in `js/common/bugFixBatchContext.js:10` slipped through every green CI run.\n\nPre-existing, but this PR deepens the gap by adding coverage to a dead file. The stale `js/unit-tests/run_bugFixBatchDevelopment.json` doesn't help either — it references legacy `agents/js/unit-tests/...` paths (from when this repo was a submodule) and is wired into nothing.\n\nSuggested fix: add `js/unit-tests/test_bugFixBatchContext`-level coverage to a wired suite — either add `js/unit-tests/test_bugFixBatchDevelopment.js` to `run_all.json` (and fix the `agents/` paths in `run_bugFixBatchDevelopment.json`), or move the shared-module tests into the already-wired `test_developBugFixBatchAndCreatePR.js`."
